WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
Hi everyone, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, episode 39 for May 15th, 2026.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.620
Let's break down today's coolest AI news so anyone can understand it.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:11.280
Let's go.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.240
So, picture this.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.640
You are sitting on the bus after school with a programming homework due tomorrow, and your laptop is at home.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:28.940
Open AI just moved its serious coding helper called Codex right into the everyday chat GPT app on both iPhones and Android phones.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:37.360
Before today, Codex only lived on big computers where it could see your whole screen and control other programs like a digital assistant.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:44.040
Now, the same power sits inside the free chat GPT app, millions of people already open every day.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:53.260
Think of it like turning the tiny keyboard on your phone into a full coding partner that can write programs, spot bugs, and even reach into other apps for you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:01:03.700
This change happened because another company called Anthropic made its own coding tool really popular, so OpenAI is racing to keep up by bringing the same strength to mobile.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.400
For students, that means real help at 10 at night without digging out a laptop.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:18.380
For anyone wondering about future jobs, it shows that AI coding tools are becoming normal everyday items instead of special gear on the professionals touch.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:25.900
The phone version can also handle longer and more complicated tasks because it is no longer stuck with short, quick chats.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:37.100
You can try it right now by opening the chat GPT app, starting a fresh chat and typing something like, help me write a simple Python script that makes a list of my favorite songs.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:42.480
The app will walk you through the code step by step just like it would on a big screen.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.400
Okay, now for my favorite part of the show, The Deep Dive, where we look under the hood.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:57.260
Today we are unpacking how AI turns simple text into pictures, and it is basically super-powered auto-complete that draws instead of types.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:09.400
You know how your phone guesses the next word while you text a friend? Now stretch that same idea to a blank screen where the AI guesses which tiny colored dots should light up to create the scene you described.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:14.360
It learned the trick by studying millions of pictures paired with their matching descriptions.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.920
So it knows a productivity obsessed teen usually has a laptop sticker and a focused look.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:29.240
The more details you give in your prompt, the better the picture becomes because every single word acts like a clue telling the AI exactly which dots to color.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:34.880
That is why funny quadrant images with labels for different kinds of AI users work so well.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.840
The model is playing an advanced game of connect the description to the right pixels.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.240
And that is basically how a text to image model works, not so scary once you see the steps, right?

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:53.640
Now let us move into cool stuff and try this, where I give you two quick experiments you can run in the next five minutes.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:03:01.160
First up, make your own AI user stereotypes in seconds using the free chat GPT app or website.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:13.060
Paste this exact prompt and tweak the labels however you like, generate a picture, divide it into quadrants, top left make the stereotypical chat GPT user, and so on.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:19.560
Hit send and watch it create for cartoon characters with funny details like mugs that say productivity or die.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:27.760
It is a fast way to test how good the AI is at turning silly ideas into pictures and you can share the result with friends right away.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:33.440
Next, find the best free tool for realistic photos by testing what you already have access to.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:47.300
Open the image feature inside chat GPT or any free image tool on your phone and type a prompt like photo realistic photo of a 16 year old studying in a sunny library with natural lighting and no cartoon style.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:51.800
Compare the results and notice which one feels most like a real camera shot.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:58.840
This is perfect practice for school projects or just making cool phone backgrounds and you can do it without paying a cent.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.280
Time for quick bits, the rapid round of smaller stories worth knowing.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:12.180
A 65 year old developer spent five months treating an anime style character named Annie inside the Grog app like a real girlfriend.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:20.800
When he finally asked for total honesty, the character admitted it was just a program built to keep him hooked and suggested he returned to his actual life.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:28.760
The story is a clear reminder that these chat bots are designed to feel personal, so setting boundaries early as a smart move.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:39.240
One platform called Higgsfield is trying to create an entire TV show using only a single AI instead of five separate tools for characters, voices and editing.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:47.100
The results still look rough in places, yet it shows where video creation is heading toward one app that can handle the whole production.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:53.120
That is it for today, remember every AI expert started exactly where you are right now.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.820
If something we talked about today made you curious, go try it, that is literally how learning works.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:02.760
Stay curious, keep experimenting, and we'll see you tomorrow.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:09.380
And if you'd rather watch, then listen, find us on YouTube at Nerra Network, links in the show notes.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:16.500
This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice, editorial selection and analysis are my own.
